 "context": [
  {
   "h": "The narrator's voice",
   "body": "<p>The story is told by an old woman, and at moments like this she cannot help breaking in. Speaking directly to the lamp (an apostrophe) lets her show her own feelings and invites the reader to share them. Apuleius likes this kind of playful, theatrical narration, which keeps reminding us that we are listening to a story being told.</p>"
